      <problem>
        <p>Mental math You can use binomial multiplication to multiply numbers without a calculator. Say you need to multiply $$13$$ times $$15.$$ Think of $$13$$ as $$10 + 3$$ and $$15$$ as $$10 + 5.$$</p>
        <list type="ol" style="1">
          <item>ⓐ Multiply $$(10 + 3)(10 + 5)$$ by the FOIL method.</item>
          <item>ⓑ Multiply $$13\ \cdot \ 15$$ without using a calculator.</item>
          <item>ⓒ Which way is easier for you? Why?</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <list type="ol" style="1">
          <item>ⓐ 195</item>
          <item>ⓑ 195</item>
          <item>ⓒ Answers will vary.</item>
        </list>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
